{
  "$comment": "The published vocabulary sets this tree last accepted. Generated by `make vocab-accept` and read by `make vocab-check`. The rules are ADR-20260827-qvk. The only field a person writes is \"key\", which names the fields identifying an entry in a new set.",
  "schema": 1,
  "taken": "2026-08-27",
  "unversioned": [
    {
      "vocabulary": "error-codes",
      "why": "sdk/fault carries no content version and no format version, so the vocabulary index publishes an empty string for it. ADR-20260825-bhe rule 3 asks for one and ADR-20260827-qvk rule 2 refuses a new vocabulary that arrives this way."
    },
    {
      "vocabulary": "extensions",
      "why": "sdk/extension carries no version for the set of registered entries, only the version each entry declares for itself."
    },
    {
      "vocabulary": "capabilities",
      "why": "sdk/connectorapi carries no version and no artefact under docs/vocabularies, so this gate cannot reach it at all."
    },
    {
      "vocabulary": "device-states",
      "why": "the set is per-install and not per-build: every entry comes from an adapter an operator installed, so ADR-20260831-nbj rule 22 gives it no artefact under docs/vocabularies and ADR-20260827-qvk rule 1 leaves its content version unmoved by a declaration. It carries a format version, because the shape of an entry is this build's own."
    }
  ],
